# hi3516cv6xx_waybeam_generic: wireless stack for the FPV link.
#
# Merged on top of hi3516cv6xx.generic.config by BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES,
# never replacing it: the base config has CONFIG_WIRELESS and CONFIG_WLAN off,
# so on this SoC family no USB WiFi adapter can exist at all. Only the symbols
# below change; NOR/FMC, MIPI/I2C, GPIO, UART, MMZ/CMA and the recovery stack
# stay exactly as the common config has them.
#
# Why it is needed: this image carries rtl8812au and rtl88x2eu for
# wifibroadcast. Both are cfg80211 drivers -- they register a wiphy and
# implement monitor mode and raw injection in their own tree -- and
# /usr/bin/wifibroadcast drives them through `iw`, which speaks nl80211 and
# nothing else. Without cfg80211 there is no wlan0 to put in monitor mode.
#
# What is deliberately NOT enabled, and why:
#
#   CONFIG_MAC80211   neither adapter is a softmac driver, so nothing here
#                     would use it; it is ~600 KB of module for no behaviour.
#                     Add CONFIG_MAC80211=m if a mac80211 part (ath9k_htc,
#                     mt7601u, ...) is ever wanted beside them.
#
#   CONFIG_CFG80211_REQUIRE_SIGNED_REGDB
#                     cfg80211 selects FW_LOADER outright, and that hidden
#                     symbol defaults to y and unconditionally selects
#                     SYSTEM_DATA_VERIFICATION -- RSA/ASN1/X509/PKCS7 plus every
#                     initramfs decompressor, ~27 KB of vmlinux. The kernel is
#                     the tight half of this layout: u-boot reads a fixed
#                     2048 KB window, post-image-split refuses to write past it,
#                     and only ~18 KB was free. It is hidden behind
#                     CFG80211_CERTIFICATION_ONUS (which needs EXPERT), so the
#                     only way to decline it is to open that submenu and say no.
#                     EXPERT itself does not change any value the base config
#                     already has; it only makes the symbols askable. And the
#                     regulator is already off: no regulatory.db is shipped
#                     (BR2_PACKAGE_WIRELESS_REGDB is not selected), so nothing
#                     would have been verified anyway.
#
#   CONFIG_CFG80211_CRDA_SUPPORT
#                     with no regdb to load, CRDA has nothing to do, and with it
#                     off cfg80211 does not even ask. The wiphy keeps the
#                     regdomain its driver sets -- both RTL trees here ship
#                     their own country-00 table -- and the wfb script's
#                     `iw reg set 00` becomes a no-op.
#
#   CONFIG_CFG80211_WEXT
#                     WEXT_CORE is `def_bool y` underneath it, which pulls the
#                     iwconfig-era shims into vmlinux (another ~2 KB) for code
#                     paths neither driver needs.

CONFIG_WIRELESS=y
CONFIG_WLAN=y
CONFIG_EXPERT=y
CONFIG_CFG80211=m
CONFIG_CFG80211_DEFAULT_PS=y
CONFIG_CFG80211_CERTIFICATION_ONUS=y
# CONFIG_CFG80211_REQUIRE_SIGNED_REGDB is not set
# CONFIG_CFG80211_USE_KERNEL_REGDB_KEYS is not set
# CONFIG_CFG80211_CRDA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_CFG80211_WEXT is not set
# CONFIG_RFKILL is not set
